From: PipOS
Subject: [PATCH] kmsdrm: scan out XRGB8888, not ARGB8888

SDL asks GBM for an ARGB8888 surface and hands that format to the kernel.
The main display plane of many drivers does not accept a format with alpha:
virtio-gpu rejects it ("Invalid pixel format AR24"), and so do Intel GPUs
before Skylake, which includes the HD 4000 this OS is built for. The mode set
then fails and nothing is ever shown.

A screen has no use for alpha. XRGB8888 is accepted everywhere.

---
--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-11-20 11:03:04.308777043 +0000
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c	2026-11-20 11:03:04.309777056 +0000
@@ -1193,7 +1193,7 @@
     SDL_VideoDisplay *display = SDL_GetDisplayForWindow(window);
     SDL_DisplayData *dispdata = (SDL_DisplayData *)display->driverdata;
 
-    uint32_t surface_fmt = GBM_FORMAT_ARGB8888;
+    uint32_t surface_fmt = GBM_FORMAT_XRGB8888;
     uint32_t surface_flags = GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT | GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING;
 
     EGLContext egl_context;
